    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\ng==\n```help\n>lua\n  print(\"something\")\n<\n```\nmessage: No code block found\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\nhelp.lua\n```lua\n  local query = vim.treesitter.query.parse(\n    'vimdoc',\n    [[\n    (codeblock\n      (language) @_lang\n      .\n      (code) @code\n      (#any-of? @_lang \"lua\" \"vim\")\n      (#set! @code lang @_lang))\n  ]]\n  )\n```\nchange to\n```lua\n  local query = vim.treesitter.query.parse(\n    'vimdoc',\n    [[\n    (codeblock\n      (language) @_lang\n      .\n      (code) @code\n      (#any-of? @_lang \"lua\\n\" \"vim\\n\")\n      (#set! @code lang @_lang))\n  ]]\n  )\n```\nOK\n---------------------------------------------------------------------\nIt might be my problem, but I really can't find it.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nnvim --clean\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1103+ge4137a7324\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\narch\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nbob install nightly",
